description:
File: rust/lichen-core/src/tdma_beacon.rs

The ParseError enum (lines 51-55) is missing std::error::Error and std::fmt::Display implementations.

Custom error types in public APIs should implement the standard error traits for:
- Composability with ? operator in functions returning Box<dyn Error> or anyhow::Error
- Integration with error handling crates (thiserror, anyhow)
- Consistent error reporting via .to_string()

Suggested fix:

impl std::fmt::Display for ParseError {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> std::fmt::Result {
        match self {
            Self::TooShort => write!(f, "beacon too short"),
            Self::ReservedFlagSet => write!(f, "reserved flag bit set"),
        }
    }
}

impl std::error::Error for ParseError {}

Or use #[derive(thiserror::Error)] if thiserror is available.
